# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The DOCKER IMAGE is the deployable artifact, so its inputs are the must-keep
# set and nothing below may match them: Dockerfile, requirements-api.txt, and
# scripts/narrate/** (the two COPY lines + the rp_handler.py CMD). Model weights
# are NOT in this repo — the build pulls them from HF into the image's own cache.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Markdown: only CLAUDE.md and README.md tracked (many per-version .md exist) ──
# No leading slash on !README.md, so scripts/README.md etc. survive too.
*.md
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md
# Session reports are deliverables, not per-version scratch docs. Must come AFTER
# the *.md line above — in gitignore the LAST matching pattern wins.
!*-report.md
# Keeps the tts-research skill + agent definitions working for clones — *.md would
# otherwise hide .claude/skills/tts-research/SKILL.md and .claude/agents/*.md, which
# are functional code, not version-history docs:
!.claude/**/*.md

# ── Corpora / built data (tts_corpus/ stays TRACKED — small source TSVs) ──
tts_data/
# has its OWN .git inside — ignoring avoids a broken gitlink on first commit
tts-research-reports/
logs/

# ── v1 / v2 / v3 dataset + output artifacts ──
marathi_dataset_v*/

# ── remaining built datasets not matched by an existing dir rule ──
mar_hin_betacraft_ds/
marathi_sunita_ds_v6/

# ── trial / A-B / narration audio output dirs (trailing slash = dirs only, so
#    scripts/narrate/narrate_gemini.py is NOT matched) ──
ab_out/
base_caption_test/
betacraft_fix/
betacraft_outputs/
gemini_*/
narrations_*/
new_test_beta_audio/
partial_audio/

# ── binary safety nets (stop a stray checkpoint hitting GitHub's 100MB limit) ──
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.onnx
*.msgpack
*.npy
*.pkl
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# ── secrets (.env holds the WEBHOOK-URL Slack key + API credentials) ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
